1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:04,962
Now implement the same business cases in Python with pytest and the synchronous

2
00:00:04,975 --> 00:00:10,888
Playwright API. The important translation is the lifecycle, not replacing camel case

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:16,312
with underscores. Each case must receive fresh data, authenticate its own browser

4
00:00:16,325 --> 00:00:22,450
context, execute its assertions, and release resources even when something fails. The

5
00:00:22,463 --> 00:00:27,912
pytest plugin already provides a page and context. Build your laboratory fixtures

6
00:00:27,925 --> 00:00:33,388
around those objects so isolation and trace options remain understandable. Keep the

7
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:36,700
same amounts, record counts, and idempotency rules.

8
00:00:38,934 --> 00:00:42,809
Open the Python test project and invoke the virtual environment's interpreter

9
00:00:42,822 --> 00:00:48,084
directly. Check the installed packages against the project's requirements, then run

10
00:00:48,096 --> 00:00:53,796
pytest with a targeted case selection. Calling Python as a module launcher ensures

11
00:00:53,809 --> 00:00:58,847
pytest comes from this environment. If your terminal finds a different Python on its

12
00:00:58,859 --> 00:01:02,847
search path, packages and browsers can appear to be missing even though another

13
00:01:02,859 --> 00:01:08,047
environment contains them. Resolve that mismatch first, and record the interpreter

14
00:01:08,059 --> 00:01:10,959
used so another learner can reproduce your execution.

15
00:01:13,184 --> 00:01:19,059
Draw two HTTP clients beside the browser. A dedicated preparation client uses the

16
00:01:19,072 --> 00:01:24,522
local test hook key to create and remove fixtures. The page's associated request

17
00:01:24,534 --> 00:01:30,134
client logs in and queries business APIs as the simulated user. Keep the hook header

18
00:01:30,146 --> 00:01:35,272
away from global browser headers. This prevents a business request from accidentally

19
00:01:35,284 --> 00:01:41,122
carrying administrative test capabilities. It also makes failures easier to classify:

20
00:01:41,359 --> 00:01:46,409
fixture creation, login, transfer submission, and observation have different expected

21
00:01:46,422 --> 00:01:48,959
responses and different evidence requirements.

22
00:01:51,178 --> 00:01:55,616
A function-scoped fixture can yield the created dataset to a test and finalize it

23
00:01:55,628 --> 00:02:00,816
afterward. The displayed skeleton explains ownership rather than providing a complete

24
00:02:00,828 --> 00:02:05,191
implementation: create data through the documented local endpoint, yield its

25
00:02:05,203 --> 00:02:10,953
identifiers, and delete that exact fixture in the finalization block. Your actual

26
00:02:10,966 --> 00:02:16,653
helper must check response statuses and handle partial setup failures. If login fails

27
00:02:16,666 --> 00:02:22,140
after creation, cleanup still owns the created fixture. Avoid a global reset that

28
00:02:22,153 --> 00:02:25,440
erases data belonging to another learner or parallel worker.

29
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:31,935
Use the context supplied by the pytest plugin and post the fixture's synthetic

30
00:02:31,948 --> 00:02:37,335
credentials through its associated request client. Assert the successful status before

31
00:02:37,348 --> 00:02:42,872
navigating. Because this request belongs to the browser context, the resulting cookie

32
00:02:42,885 --> 00:02:48,710
becomes available to the page. An independently created HTTP client has separate

33
00:02:48,723 --> 00:02:53,723
cookie storage unless you deliberately transfer state. Keep this choice visible in the

34
00:02:53,735 --> 00:02:59,072
fixture instead of hiding it in a utility with unclear ownership. Always identify

35
00:02:59,085 --> 00:03:01,360
whose session the browser is actually using.

36
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:08,178
Inside the successful transfer test, navigate and select the fixture's account and

37
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:13,965
beneficiary before entering one hundred pesos. The excerpt focuses on submission once

38
00:03:13,978 --> 00:03:19,603
those selections exist. Python's synchronous API does not require JavaScript await

39
00:03:19,615 --> 00:03:25,090
expressions. Use Playwright's expectation object for UI assertions so the intended

40
00:03:25,103 --> 00:03:30,253
text condition can settle. A plain immediate text comparison has different waiting

41
00:03:30,265 --> 00:03:35,953
behavior. When asking AI to translate the test, require the synchronous API

42
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:40,765
throughout; mixing synchronous and asynchronous patterns produces failures unrelated

43
00:03:40,778 --> 00:03:41,778
to the business rule.

44
00:03:44,008 --> 00:03:49,271
Observe the account using the authenticated page request client. In Python, the

45
00:03:49,283 --> 00:03:55,421
response status in this example is a property, while parsing JSON uses a method. These

46
00:03:55,433 --> 00:04:00,358
small language differences are easy for generated code to get wrong. Assert the

47
00:04:00,371 --> 00:04:06,158
successful HTTP status, then the integer balance. Apply the same pattern to the

48
00:04:06,171 --> 00:04:11,246
canonical transfer collection and inspect its count and fields. For the separate

49
00:04:11,258 --> 00:04:15,383
distributed ledger view, use bounded polling rather than assuming that its record

50
00:04:15,396 --> 00:04:17,658
appears immediately after account settlement.

51
00:04:19,890 --> 00:04:25,265
For insufficient funds, prepare eleven hundred pesos in a fresh fixture. Enter the

52
00:04:25,278 --> 00:04:29,802
response expectation context before clicking, and match the transfer request

53
00:04:29,815 --> 00:04:35,628
specifically. After the context closes, inspect the captured response, its business

54
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:40,628
error code, and the UI alert. Then prove the balance and transfer count stayed

55
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:45,852
unchanged. This distinguishes a business rejection from a button that never submitted

56
00:04:45,865 --> 00:04:51,852
anything. A locator timeout, a network failure, and an insufficient funds response are

57
00:04:51,865 --> 00:04:55,652
different observations and should not become one generic rejection result.

58
00:04:57,884 --> 00:05:02,896
Create the request body and idempotency key once within the Python case, then submit

59
00:05:02,909 --> 00:05:08,159
the same values twice through the authenticated context. Check creation followed by

60
00:05:08,172 --> 00:05:13,696
replay, compare the identifiers, and assert one debit and one record. If you

61
00:05:13,709 --> 00:05:18,446
parameterize cases later, keep the fixture function-scoped so each parameter receives

62
00:05:18,459 --> 00:05:24,296
independent data. A parameter list describes inputs; it does not automatically isolate

63
00:05:24,309 --> 00:05:29,771
the state those inputs mutate. Inspect resulting test names so failures identify the

64
00:05:29,784 --> 00:05:31,734
business case and dataset used.

65
00:05:33,958 --> 00:05:38,933
Run the Python suite with trace retention on failure and request a JUnit XML result

66
00:05:38,946 --> 00:05:44,733
file. The plugin's trace options apply to its managed fixtures; a browser context

67
00:05:44,746 --> 00:05:49,970
created manually in a helper needs its own trace management. That is why we extended

68
00:05:49,983 --> 00:05:55,620
the provided fixtures. Inspect an actual failed run to confirm the trace exists and

69
00:05:55,633 --> 00:06:01,083
can be opened. A configuration line expresses intended behavior, while a saved

70
00:06:01,095 --> 00:06:05,546
artifact demonstrates that it occurred. Keep those statements separate in your

71
00:06:05,558 --> 00:06:06,746
execution report.

72
00:06:08,976 --> 00:06:14,088
Review fixture finalization after a deliberately failing assertion. Cleanup should

73
00:06:14,101 --> 00:06:18,938
attempt to remove only the owned dataset and release its preparation client. If

74
00:06:18,951 --> 00:06:23,588
cleanup also fails, report that problem with the fixture identifier without replacing

75
00:06:23,601 --> 00:06:28,588
the original assertion failure. Save evidence before destroying the context or

76
00:06:28,601 --> 00:06:34,113
deleting data needed for inspection. For an interrupted process, record outstanding

77
00:06:34,126 --> 00:06:39,588
fixture identifiers so a later recovery step can target them. Reliable teardown

78
00:06:39,601 --> 00:06:43,988
belongs to the experiment's design, rather than being a cosmetic action after the

79
00:06:44,001 --> 00:06:45,113
assertions finish.

80
00:06:47,330 --> 00:06:52,742
Finish by drawing the dependency graph for one Python test. The preparation client

81
00:06:52,755 --> 00:06:57,630
creates the dataset; the dataset and browser context establish authentication; the

82
00:06:57,642 --> 00:07:03,305
page performs the action; API observations verify effects; finalizers release what

83
00:07:03,317 --> 00:07:09,130
they own. Point to the code that guarantees each transition. Then report the actual

84
00:07:09,142 --> 00:07:14,805
status of the three cases, including blocked setup or remaining failures. You now have

85
00:07:14,817 --> 00:07:18,455
a Python structure that preserves the TypeScript version's business meaning while

86
00:07:18,467 --> 00:07:21,755
using pytest's own lifecycle and reporting conventions.
